<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; ">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; ">There are no market-related
performance conditions or non-vesting conditions that should be considered for determining the fair value of options.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; ">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; ">Moolec Science estimates
an expected rotation of <ix:nonFraction contextRef="c0" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="mlec:ConstantValuePercentage" scale="-2" unitRef="pure" id="ixv-7929">2.00</ix:nonFraction>% annually at constant value, taking into account historical patterns of executives maintaining their jobs
and the probability of exercising the options. This estimate is reviewed at the end of each annual or interim period.</p></ix:nonNumeric><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; ">&#160;</p><div>


