<td style="width: 0in"/><td style="width: 0.25in; text-align: left"><span style="font-size: 10pt">(1</span>)</td><td style="text-align: justify"><ix:footnote id="ix_13_footnote" xml:lang="en-US">As of December 31, 2024, the Company recognized an income of
$<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c112" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:ExpenseFromSharebasedPaymentTransactionsInWhichGoodsOrServicesReceivedDidNotQualifyForRecognitionAsAssets" scale="6" unitRef="usd" id="ixv-8112">0.6</ix:nonFraction> million related to the reversal of previously recognized share-based payment expenses. This adjustment arose due to the non-fulfillment
of specific performance milestones required for some participants to earn the associated benefits under the share-based compensation
plan whose first milestone was to be measured as of December 31, 2024. As a result, the previously accrued expense was reversed in accordance
with IFRS 2 &#8211; <i>Share-based Payment</i>, recognizing the corresponding impact in the statement of profit or loss under <i>administrative
expenses</i>.</ix:footnote></td>
